(vector (map (:adr/consequences (vector "single authoritative reference for org taxonomy — supersedes the inline 公益/事業 mentions in library ADRs" "new-repo placement decided by axis: any library -> kotoba-lang; agent+公益 -> etzhayyim; product+ビジネス -> gftdcojp; cloud+data -> com-junkawasaki" "com-junkawasaki -> kotoba-lang full -clj migration DECIDED (2026-06-30); language-core already moved, generic -clj infra to follow; com-junkawasaki end-state = cloud + data + Jun Kawasaki personal/private research projects (amended 2026-07-19, see Amendment section)" "codified in repos.edn as a doc-only :orgs key (generator does not read it, mirroring :manifest-workflow)" "individual/vendor-specific service repos now classified BEFORE scaffolding via :repo-creation-check, not retroactively at migration time" "noted exception (2026-07-01, ADR-2607012100): cloud-itonami-* public OSS business/occupation blueprint repos (35, formerly under gftdcojp) live in a dedicated cloud-itonami org — a product-line-specific public repo home, not a 5th taxonomy tier; the 4-org role split above is unchanged")), (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "which GitHub org a new repo belongs in: any library (language or -clj infra) -> kotoba-lang / public-interest agent -> etzhayyim / commercial product -> gftdcojp / cloud+data -> com-junkawasaki" "the 公益=etzhayyim / 事業=gftdcojp split that library ADRs assert only inline" "com-junkawasaki -> kotoba-lang full -clj migration (decided 2026-06-30); com-junkawasaki end-state = cloud + data + personal/private research (amended 2026-07-19)" "repo-creation-time placement check for individual/vendor-specific services: layer test (kotoba-lang) then 3-axis+Charter Rider check (etzhayyim vs gftdcojp) — amendment 2026-07-01")), (:adr/supersedes (vector)), (:adr/superseded_by (vector "adr-2607289700-org-taxonomy-by-invocation-axis-network-awai")), (:adr/topic "org-taxonomy"), (:adr/related (vector "manifest/repos.edn" "CLAUDE.md" "90-docs/adr/2606272212-ci-clj-github-actions-edn-dag.edn" "90-docs/adr/2606272209-policy-clj-abac-rbac-edn.edn" "90-docs/adr/2606272213-ddl-clj-sql-schema-migration.edn" "90-docs/adr/2606272200-bpmn-clj-edn-process-library.edn" "90-docs/adr/2606301900-isco-cofog-organism-actors.edn" "90-docs/adr/2606272237-manifest-workflow-single-entry-commit.edn" "orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-stripe/NOT-MIGRATED-VENDOR-REGULATORY.md.edn" "orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-livecam/NOT-MIGRATED-CHARTER-VIOLATION.md.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607012100-cloud-itonami-org-split.edn")), (:adr/status "superseded"), (:adr/id "adr-2606302300-org-taxonomy-4-orgs"), (:adr/repo-creation-check "{:amended \"2026-07-01\", :purpose \"answer 'which org does a NEW repo go in' at creation time, before scaffolding\", :step-1-layer-test {:question \"is this a pure technical layer: .cljc, zero network I/O, zero vendor SDK, records/protocol/data-model only?\", :yes \"kotoba-lang\", :exemplars [\"banking\" \"card\" \"swift\" \"eth-crypto\" \"cacao\" \"did\" \"vc\" \"koe (ports + dialog-loop only; every concrete capability injected by host, so admissible despite service-shaped domain)\"], :no \"fails layer test -> go to step-2 (this covers: real PayPay/Stripe/bank API calls, a video-call app, a wallet UI, an Ethereum RPC client, ...)\"}, :step-2-3-axis-charter-check {:when \"candidate is an individual/vendor-specific service (fails step-1)\", :worked-examples [\"orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-stripe/NOT-MIGRATED-VENDOR-REGULATORY.md.edn\" \"orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-livecam/NOT-MIGRATED-CHARTER-VIOLATION.md.edn\"], :axis-a-settlement-regulatory {:question \"does the service hit a Settlement/regulatory axis? (PCI-DSS, 資金決済法, 景品表示法, 特定商取引法, KYC/AML, banking/broker-dealer licensing, ...)\", :if-hit \"gftdcojp/ai-gftd-* (vendor-retained; regulatory liability stays with the gftd business entity)\"}, :axis-b-charter-rider-v2 {:question \"does the business model or content type hit Charter Rider v2.0 §2(a-h)?\", :clauses [\"(a) WEAPONS AND MILITARY\" \"(b) SPECULATIVE FINANCE\" \"(c) SURVEILLANCE CAPITALISM (ad-tech / data brokerage)\" \"(d) FOSSIL FUEL EXTRACTION (new projects)\" \"(e) SPECIALIST GATEKEEPING\" \"(f) MULTI-GENERATIONAL HARM\" \"(g) STRICT INDIVIDUALIST ONTOLOGY\" \"(h) WELLBECOMING SUBORDINATION VIOLATION\"], :if-hit \"gftdcojp/ai-gftd-* (excluded from etzhayyim by charter, same as ai-gftd-livecam)\"}, :neither-hit \"etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-* as a proper actor (sealed-intelligence dashv independent governor, append-only ledger, RAD identity per CLAUDE.md Actors section); consumes kotoba-lang protocol libs for the technical layer\"}}"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-19"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2606302300: Four-org taxonomy (kotoba-lang / etzhayyim / gftdcojp / com-junkawasaki)\n\n**Status**: superseded by ADR-2607289700 (2026-07-28)\n**Date**: 2026-06-30\n\n> **2026-07-28**: ADR-2607289700 replaced this in full. It moved the classifying axis off *purpose* (公益 / 事業) onto *起動主体 x 事業主体* (who starts the thing x whose business it is), because purpose does not determine implementation and the split measured as broken: etzhayyim held 466 libraries out of 612 repos, so asking whether a repo is public-interest said nothing about what it is. The org set changed too (network-awai and cloud-itonami added, jk-luxury dissolved), the `ai-gftd-` prefix rule was abolished (D4), and the Charter half of `:adr/repo-creation-check` below was replaced by D3. The four-org table and the migration decision stay here as the record of what was decided on 2026-06-30 — they are not current placement rules.\n\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n## Context\n\nThe superproject partitions work across four GitHub orgs checked out under\n`orgs/<org>/`. The split has been **implicit** until now — referenced in passing\nby many library ADRs (\"最初の消費者は別 org(**公益=etzhayyim / 事業=gftdcojp**)\nの actor が …\") and encoded structurally in `manifest/repos.edn`\n(`:remotes`, `:path-overrides`, `:extra-projects`) — but never recorded as a\nsingle authoritative taxonomy. This ADR writes it down so new repos land in the\nright org by design, not by accident.\n\n## Decision\n\nFour orgs, partitioned along two axes — **what kind of thing** (language /\nagent / human-facing product / platform) and, for actors/products only,\n**for whom** (公益 public-interest / ビジネス business):\n\n| org | role (what) | scope (whom) | west remote | ~projects |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `kotoba-lang` | **kotoba 言語** — pure-CLJC language/core libraries & tech (`kotoba`, `kotoba-code`, `kasane`, `kami-*`, `murakumo`, `office-*`, `svgraph`, …) + (migrating) all generic `-clj` infra | language substrate, consumed by all orgs | `git@github.com:kotoba-lang` | 85→growing |\n| `etzhayyim` | **agent-centric** — dispatchable organism actors (`com-etzhayyim-*`, one per UNSPSC / ISCO / COFOG code) | **公益 (public-interest)** | `github.com/etzhayyim` | 170 |\n| `gftdcojp` | **human-centric** — human-facing products & business services (`ai-gftd-*`, apps, HR `talent`) | **ビジネス (business)** | `git@github.com:gftdcojp` | 50 |\n| `com-junkawasaki` | **transitional foundation** — generic `-clj` infra **migrating fully to `kotoba-lang`** (decided); retains cloud control planes + heavy/data projects + Jun Kawasaki personal/private research | Jun Kawasaki platform/foundation (origin org) | `git@github.com:com-junkawasaki` | 53→shrinking |\n\n### Axes\n\n1. **What**: `kotoba-lang` is the *language/substrate* (and, after migration,\n   the home of all `-clj` infrastructure libraries); `etzhayyim` and `gftdcojp`\n   are *agents/products* built on it; `com-junkawasaki` is being *emptied of\n   libraries* into `kotoba-lang`.\n2. **Whom (actors/products only)**: `etzhayyim` = 公益 (common-good services\n   delivered as agents); `gftdcojp` = ビジネス (commercial). The 公益/事業\n   distinction was previously only asserted inline by the library ADRs\n   (ci-clj, ddl-clj, policy-clj, bpmn-clj); this ADR is now its authority.\n\n### Migration (com-junkawasaki → kotoba-lang) — DECIDED\n\nOwner decision (2026-06-30): **the generic infrastructure `-clj` libraries\nfully migrate to `kotoba-lang`**, using the same `repos.edn :path-overrides`\nmechanism as the language-core.\n\n- **Already migrated** (language-core): `kotoba`, `kotoba-code`, `kasane`,\n  `kami-*`, `murakumo`, `office-*`, `svgraph`, `aiueos`, `kekkai`, `utsushi`,\n  `vehicle-design-actor` → `kami-engine-vehicle-designer`, …\n- **To migrate** (generic `-clj` infra): `aero-clj`, `bpmn-clj`, `ci-clj`,\n  `ddl-clj`, `dmn-clj`, `crash-clj`, `cron-clj`, `datom-clj`, `graphql-clj`,\n  `ical-clj`, `jsonlogic-clj`, `kagi-clj`, `kenchi-clj`, `kotobase-clj`, …\n  (full inventory to be enumerated in the migration PR).\n- **`com-junkawasaki` end-state**: **cloud control planes** (`cloud-manimani`,\n  `cloud-murakumo`) + **heavy/data projects** (`spirit-in-physics`,\n  `ghosthacker`) + **Jun Kawasaki personal/private research projects**\n  (amended 2026-07-19 — see Amendment section below). All generic-infra\n  libraries will have left for `kotoba-lang`; personal/private research is a\n  separate, standing category that is not part of that migration.\n\n### Exception: SVG-era Office tooling restored to com-junkawasaki\n\nResolved 2026-07-01 in ADR-2607011100: the CLJ/EDN rewrites remain in\n`kotoba-lang` (`office`, `svgraph`), but the legacy SVG-era browser/TypeScript\ntooling is restored as separate `com-junkawasaki` repos:\n`com-junkawasaki/office-causal` and `com-junkawasaki/svgraph`. This is an\nexplicit exception to the general library migration rule because those repos\npreserve package names, GitHub Pages URLs, and SVG/Office integration surfaces\nthat should not be conflated with the kotoba CLJ/EDN substrate.\n\nMechanism: add `<x>-clj` → `<x>` entries to `:path-overrides`; regenerate\n(`nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs`) + `west update` to relocate checkouts;\nverify `--check` canonical and `pin == repo HEAD`. GitHub org relocation per\nrepo is a separate decision (some repos may stay at `github.com/com-junkawasaki`\nand be checked out under `kotoba-lang/` via `:remote-overrides`, as\n`kami-engine-sdk` already is).\n\n### Out of scope (not west-managed)\n\nPersonal / operational data lives **outside** west and is **not** part of this\ntaxonomy:\n\n- `orgs/kawasakijun/` — personal ops/state (finances, goals, litigation, KPIs).\n- `orgs/personal/` — life-data vault (mail, photos, takeout, accounts).\n\n## Consequences\n\n- **New-repo placement rule**:\n  - **any library / substrate** (language or `-clj` infra) → `kotoba-lang`\n  - public-interest agent → `etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-*`\n  - commercial product / actor → `gftdcojp/ai-gftd-*` (or `app-*`)\n  - cloud control plane / heavy data → `com-junkawasaki` (the only thing that\n    stays here once migration completes)\n\n  Enforced through the standing \"new project\" workflow (CLAUDE.md) and the\n  doc-only `:orgs` key in `repos.edn`.\n- `:path-overrides` is the migration mechanism; `gen-west-manifest.cljs --check`\n  keeps `west.yml` canonical.\n- This ADR is the single reference for the org taxonomy; the passing 公益/事業\n  mentions in library ADRs now resolve here.\n\n## Decisions (resolved 2026-06-30)\n\n- **`com-junkawasaki` end-state**: the generic `-clj` infrastructure libraries\n  **fully migrate to `kotoba-lang`** (same `:path-overrides` mechanism as the\n  language-core). `com-junkawasaki` will retain **cloud control planes\n  (cloud-manimani, cloud-murakumo) + heavy/data projects (spirit-in-physics,\n  ghosthacker) + Jun Kawasaki personal/private research projects** (amended\n  2026-07-19 — see Amendment section below; this category was omitted from\n  the original 2026-06-30 decision). Migration in progress; tracked via `repos.edn\n  :path-overrides`.\n\n## Amendment (2026-07-01): repo-creation-time placement check\n\nThe \"what\" axis (§Axes 1) was previously judged informally (\"does this look\nlike a library?\"). Formalize it into a decision procedure run **before**\nscaffolding any new repo, not after:\n\n**Step 1 — layer test (kotoba-lang admission).** A candidate belongs in\n`kotoba-lang` only if it is a **pure technical layer**: `.cljc`, zero network\nI/O, zero vendor SDK, models records/protocol/data only (cf. `banking`,\n`card`, `swift`, `eth-crypto`, `cacao`, `did`, `vc`, `koe` — the last defines\nports + a dialog loop but injects every concrete capability from the host,\nso it stays admissible even though its domain, voice telephony, is\nservice-shaped). The moment a repo needs to *actually call* PayPay/Stripe/a\nbank API/a WebRTC SFU/an Ethereum RPC node, it fails this test and moves to\nstep 2.\n\n**Step 2 — 3-axis + Charter Rider check (etzhayyim vs gftdcojp).** For any\nindividual/vendor-specific service (real API integration, a video-call app,\na payment rail client, a wallet UI, …), run the same classification already\napplied during the gftdcojp→etzhayyim migration (see\n`orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-stripe/NOT-MIGRATED-VENDOR-REGULATORY.md.edn` and\n`orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-livecam/NOT-MIGRATED-CHARTER-VIOLATION.md.edn` for the\nworked examples) **at creation time, not retroactively**:\n\n  1. **3-axis regulatory/settlement check** — does the service hit a\n     Settlement/regulatory axis (PCI-DSS, 資金決済法, 景品表示法・特定商取引法,\n     KYC/AML, banking/broker-dealer licensing, …)? If yes →\n     `gftdcojp/ai-gftd-*` (vendor-retained; regulatory liability sits with\n     the gftd business entity, not the public-interest actor mesh).\n  2. **Charter Rider v2.0 §2(a–h) check** — does the business model or\n     content type hit any of WEAPONS/MILITARY, SPECULATIVE FINANCE,\n     SURVEILLANCE CAPITALISM (ad-tech/data brokerage), FOSSIL FUEL\n     EXTRACTION, SPECIALIST GATEKEEPING, MULTI-GENERATIONAL HARM, STRICT\n     INDIVIDUALIST ONTOLOGY, or WELLBECOMING SUBORDINATION? If yes →\n     `gftdcojp/ai-gftd-*` (excluded from etzhayyim by charter, same as\n     `ai-gftd-livecam`).\n  3. If **neither** axis hits → `etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-*` as a proper\n     actor (sealed-intelligence ⊣ independent governor, append-only ledger,\n     RAD identity — per the Actors section of `CLAUDE.md`), consuming\n     `kotoba-lang` protocol libraries for the technical layer.\n\nThis makes the org choice for a new individual-service repo a **two-step,\nanswerable-before-scaffolding** check instead of a taxonomy migration done\nafter the fact. Encoded machine-readably in the companion `.edn` under\n`:repo-creation-check`.\n\n## Amendment (2026-07-01): noted exception — `cloud-itonami` org\n\nADR-2607012100 moved the 35 `cloud-itonami-*` public OSS business/occupation\nblueprint repos (formerly `gftdcojp`, public) to a dedicated `cloud-itonami`\norg. This is **not** a 5th taxonomy tier: the four org roles above are\nunchanged, and `cloud-itonami` exists solely as the public-repo home for the\n`cloud-itonami-*` product line (fork-away business/occupation blueprints,\ndistinct in kind from `gftdcojp`'s own commercial `ai-gftd-*` products and\nfrom the private `cloud-itonami` business-os base repo, which stays under\n`gftdcojp`). Future `cloud-itonami-*` blueprint repos may be created directly\nunder `cloud-itonami` without transiting `gftdcojp` first.\n\n## Amendment (2026-07-04): `cloud-manimani` / `cloud-murakumo` already transferred to `gftdcojp`\n\nThe \"com-junkawasaki end-state\" text above (§Migration, §Decisions) still reads\n\"cloud control planes (cloud-manimani, cloud-murakumo)\" as staying under\n`com-junkawasaki` — that is stale. Both were GitHub-transferred to `gftdcojp`\non 2026-07-02 (`manifest/repos.edn` `:path-overrides` note, line ~29/57);\n`cloud-murakumo` was renamed to `cloud-murakumo-fleet` on transfer to avoid\ncolliding with the pre-existing `gftdcojp/cloud-murakumo` (Sora, the GPU\nserverless product). ADR-2607041302 formalizes the resulting three-repo\n`murakumo` family (`kotoba-lang/murakumo` common lib/CLI,\n`gftdcojp/cloud-murakumo` Sora, `gftdcojp/cloud-murakumo-fleet` → proposed\nrename to `gftdcojp/local-murakumo`) and is now the authority for that naming;\nthis ADR's org-taxonomy table is unaffected (both remain `gftdcojp`-owned\ncloud control planes, not `com-junkawasaki`).\n\n## Amendment (2026-07-19): com-junkawasaki also retains Jun Kawasaki personal/private research\n\nOwner correction: the \u00a72026-06-30 decision scoped `com-junkawasaki`'s end-state to\n**cloud control planes + heavy/data projects only**, omitting a category that was\nalways intended to stay \u2014 **Jun Kawasaki's personal/private research and\nformalization projects** (non-library, not owned by an etzhayyim/gftdcojp\nactor/product). The generic `-clj` infra \u2192 `kotoba-lang` migration itself is\nunaffected and remains decided; only the *end-state scope* of `com-junkawasaki`\nwidens from cloud+data-only to **cloud + data + personal/private research**.\nPlacement rule addition: a from-scratch personal research effort that fails the\nkotoba-lang library layer test (not a reusable `.cljc` substrate) and is not an\netzhayyim/gftdcojp actor or product belongs in `com-junkawasaki`. Example:\n`com-junkawasaki/iut-lean` (Lean 4 formalization research, 2026-07-19)."), (:adr/decision "{:axes [{:axis \"what (kind of thing)\", :values [\"library / substrate (kotoba-lang) — language core + all -clj infra after migration\" \"agent/product (etzhayyim, gftdcojp)\" \"cloud control plane / heavy data (com-junkawasaki, post-migration)\"]} {:axis \"whom (actors/products only)\", :values [\"公益 public-interest = etzhayyim\" \"ビジネス business = gftdcojp\"]}], :orgs {\"kotoba-lang\" {:role :language-substrate, :role-text \"kotoba 言語 + (after migration) all generic -clj infra libraries\", :scope \"language/infra substrate, consumed by all orgs\", :remote \"git@github.com:kotoba-lang\", :projects \"85 -> growing\"}, \"etzhayyim\" {:role :agent-centric, :role-text \"dispatchable organism actors (com-etzhayyim-*, UNSPSC/ISCO/COFOG)\", :scope \"公益 (public-interest)\", :remote \"github.com/etzhayyim\", :projects 170}, \"gftdcojp\" {:role :human-centric, :role-text \"human-facing products & business services (ai-gftd-*, apps, talent)\", :scope \"ビジネス (business)\", :remote \"git@github.com:gftdcojp\", :projects 50}, \"com-junkawasaki\" {:role :transitional-foundation, :role-text \"generic -clj infra migrating fully to kotoba-lang; retains cloud control planes + heavy/data + Jun Kawasaki personal/private research (amended 2026-07-19)\", :scope \"Jun Kawasaki origin org; end-state = cloud + data + personal/private research\", :remote \"git@github.com:com-junkawasaki\", :projects \"53 -> shrinking\"}}, :placement-rule {:any-library \"kotoba-lang (language core OR generic -clj infra)\", :public-interest-agent \"etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-*\", :commercial-product \"gftdcojp/ai-gftd-* or app-*\", :cloud-or-heavy-data \"com-junkawasaki (cloud + heavy-data + Jun Kawasaki personal/private research, amended 2026-07-19)\"}, :migration {:mechanism \"repos.edn :path-overrides (com-junkawasaki/<x>-clj -> kotoba-lang/<x>) + :remote-overrides where GitHub org stays\", :moved \"kotoba-language-core: kotoba, kotoba-code, kasane, kami-*, murakumo, office-*, svgraph, aiueos, kekkai, utsushi, vehicle-design-actor...\", :to-migrate \"generic -clj infra: aero-clj, bpmn-clj, ci-clj, ddl-clj, dmn-clj, crash-clj, cron-clj, datom-clj, graphql-clj, ical-clj, jsonlogic-clj, kagi-clj, kenchi-clj, kotobase-clj, ...\", :decided \"generic -clj infra FULLY migrates to kotoba-lang (owner decision 2026-06-30); com-junkawasaki end-state = data (spirit-in-physics, ghosthacker) + Jun Kawasaki personal/private research projects (amended 2026-07-19) — cloud-manimani/cloud-murakumo already GitHub-transferred to gftdcojp 2026-07-02 (superseded; see amendment-2026-07-04 below and ADR-2607041302)\", :github-org-relocation \"per-repo decision; some stay at github.com/com-junkawasaki and check out under kotoba-lang/ via :remote-overrides (cf. kami-engine-sdk)\"}, :exceptions [{:id \"adr-2607011100-svg-era-office-repo-split\", :date \"2026-07-01\", :summary \"CLJ/EDN rewrites remain in kotoba-lang, but SVG-era browser/TypeScript tooling is restored as com-junkawasaki/office-causal and com-junkawasaki/svgraph.\", :repos [\"com-junkawasaki/office-causal\" \"com-junkawasaki/svgraph\"], :reason \"preserve package names, GitHub Pages URLs, and SVG/Office integration surfaces without conflating them with the kotoba CLJ/EDN substrate\"} {:id \"adr-2607041302-murakumo-family-naming\", :date \"2026-07-04\", :summary \"cloud-manimani/cloud-murakumo (the com-junkawasaki cloud control planes named in :migration :decided above) were already GitHub-transferred to gftdcojp 2026-07-02; cloud-murakumo was renamed cloud-murakumo-fleet on transfer (collided with pre-existing gftdcojp/cloud-murakumo, Sora). ADR-2607041302 formalizes the resulting murakumo family and proposes renaming cloud-murakumo-fleet -> local-murakumo.\", :repos [\"gftdcojp/cloud-manimani\" \"gftdcojp/cloud-murakumo\" \"gftdcojp/cloud-murakumo-fleet\" \"kotoba-lang/murakumo\"], :reason \"org-taxonomy table (both gftdcojp-owned cloud control planes) is unaffected; this only corrects the stale com-junkawasaki attribution and hands naming authority to ADR-2607041302\"}], :out-of-scope {:not-west-managed [\"orgs/kawasakijun/ (personal ops/state)\" \"orgs/personal/ (life-data vault)\"]}}"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/open-questions (vector)), (:adr/problem "{:source \"owner clarification 2026-06-30\", :gap \"org partition existed only implicitly — passing 公益/事業 refs in library ADRs plus structural repos.edn keys; no single authoritative taxonomy\", :risk \"new repos land in the wrong org by accident; migration scope (com-junkawasaki->kotoba-lang) ambiguous\"}"), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2606302300: Four-org taxonomy — kotoba-lang (language) / etzhayyim (agent+公益) / gftdcojp (human+ビジネス) / com-junkawasaki (foundation→cloud+data)"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))